 Schur), k=1 for full cells, geometry finding

- dense_fixed_port_schur / produce_tet10_label / run_tet10_label_gates: Pardiso with 1024-column chunks by default,
  SuperLU fallback when pypardiso is missing. G0 k=1 benchmark: SuperLU 718+2222 s vs Pardiso 3+30 s, |dS| 4e-14.
- STRATUM_PRESETS: full cells at k=1 / size 0.05 (k=2 kept as convergence reference).
- ADDENDUM_04 section 0: the cell geometry carries 1/32 solid plates on all box faces (46% of G0 material), not part of
  the intended sheet-TPMS design; population run blocked until the geometry front-end produces the true sheet solid.
- Receipts: G0 k=1 (SuperLU 2826 s and Pardiso 83 s, both PASS), G0 k=2 reference (PASS, 105 min), solver benchmark.
